course: dictionary
lesson: 13029
title: Fae: a word with two meanings
level: primary-4
stars: 0
explain: Some words change meaning depending on where they are used. Fae is one of them. In fantasy stories, the fae are fairies. In Scots, fae means «from». Context tells you which meaning to pick. «The fae danced under the silver moon in the forest.» Fairies dancing under the moon fits the fantasy meaning, so this is the fairy meaning.
explain: Now read: «I'm fae Glasgow, so I know the city well.» Fairies cannot be from Glasgow, so fae must mean something else here. Try swapping in from: «I'm from Glasgow, so I know the city well» still makes sense. The swap check tells you fae means from.
explain: Fae is a Scots word, so you may hear it in Scotland or in films set there. In fantasy books you will often see fae magic or the fae folk. Look at the words around fae first, and they will usually tell you which meaning it has.
fact: Fae means fairies or fairy folk in fantasy stories and legends, especially Celtic tales.
fact: Fae can also describe something that belongs to the fairies, such as fae magic.
fact: In Scots, fae means «from», as in «I'm fae Glasgow».
fact: Fae is a noun in fantasy stories and a preposition in Scots.
fact: A few people use fae as a name or a pronoun, but this is rare.
exercise: «The fae danced in a ring under the silver moon.» What are the fae in this sentence? | Clouds drifting across the sky | Owls that hoot at night | Teachers in the school hall | *Fairies or fairy folk
exercise: Ella hears a friend say, «I'm fae Glasgow.» What does fae mean here? | *From | Fairy | Friend | Fast
exercise: «The fae magic turned the old oak tree silver.» What does fae magic mean? | *Magic belonging to fairies | A very tired magician | Magic from Scotland | A school magic show
test: «The fae folk lived deep in the forest, where nobody went.» What does fae mean here? | *Fairies | Lazy | From | Brave
test: «I'm fae Edinburgh, and I love the castle.» Which word could you swap in for fae? | *From | Fairy | Tall | Angry
exam: Which sentence uses fae to mean «from»? | The fae sang softly in the glen. | The fae magic made the flowers glow. | *I'm fae Glasgow, so I know the city well. | The fae were hiding behind the tree.
